entry.summary:
You've got one CRM integration in production and it's been fine for months. Now there's a second one to wire up. Same contract, same schema, same node shape. Should be a couple of days. You pull the first payload from CRM B and put it next to CRM A out of habit. CRM A, a monetary field: { "key": "estimated_cost", "value": 1275.43, "spec": { "type": "number", "format": "decimal" } }
CRM B, same kind of field: { "key": "amount", "value": "6624", "spec": { "type": "number" } }
Huh. One's a JSON number. One's a string. One tags the format, one doesn't. Both say "type": "number". And every validator between those adapters and your UI is perfectly happy with both. This is the part that takes a minute to sit with. You go looking for who got it wrong, and nobody did. Go read the contract. It say…
